<title>SOUTH AFRICA: BENCO INTERIM SHR RISES, NO DIV.</title>
<headline>BENCO INTERIM SHR RISES, NO DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended November 30,</p>
<p>1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	1.09	vs    3.24 loss</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    0.68	vs    1.98</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    0.47	vs    1.98</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.19	vs    nil </p>
<p>    Interest paid	    1.14	vs    2.01</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	0.23	vs    0.12</p>
<p>    Carats produced	 1,008	vs    2,262 </p>
<p>Full name: Benguela Concessions Ltd (mining - diamonds)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said up to February 25 a total of 2,400</p>
<p>carats had been recovered in all phases of its joint venture</p>
<p>project with Moonstone Diamonds (SA) (Pty) Ltd, a unit of</p>
<p>Moonstone Diamond Corporation NL , and the budgeted</p>
<p>figure of 2,000 carats for February had been achieved. </p>
<p>It said it intended to increase production over the next</p>
<p>three months to 5,000 carats per month.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
